<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela oil unions to join national strike.</title>
<headline>Venezuela oil unions to join national strike.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela's 60,000-strong oil union members will join a national strike called for August 6, said Carlos Ortega, president of the main oil union Fedepetrol, in a short telephone interview with Reuters on Wednesday.</p>
<p>But he was not sure if the action would affect the country's 3.2 million barrel per day oil production.</p>
<p>Ortega said members of the Fedepetrol and Fetrahidrocarburos unions would join the action, called by the Confederation of Venezuelan Workers (CTV) to protest against rises in the price of gasoline and late payment of salary increases.</p>
<p>&quot;All our members will participate,&quot; Ortega said.</p>
<p>((-- Tom Ashby, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2611))</p>
